# 1. Overall DB Health Assessment

## Current State Observations

| Issue | Impact | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| `created_by` / `updated_by` always "system" | Audit trail is useless — no user identity | HIGH |
| `namespace` column not populating in components | Deployment validation broken | HIGH |
| `cluster_environment` always null | Dead column, wasted space | MEDIUM |
| `active_deployment` in components — likely unused | Misleading data | MEDIUM |
| `gh_error` in components — purpose unclear | May be needed for error tracking | MEDIUM |
| `overlay_status` in components — purpose unclear | Dead or misunderstood column | MEDIUM |
| `scan_jobs` + `scan_runs` duplicating concerns | Unnecessary complexity | MEDIUM |
| Multiple tables serving no clear purpose | Schema noise, confusion | MEDIUM |
| No foreign key enforcement (H2 in-memory) | Referential integrity risks | LOW (fix at PostgreSQL migration) |
| K8s timestamps not environment-specific | Wrong data model | HIGH |

## Guiding Principles for This Restructure

```
1. Components table = environment-agnostic master metadata per component per fix version
2. Deployment Readiness table = environment-specific K8s data per component
3. If data exists in YAML config → do NOT duplicate in DB
4. If a table has no clear consumer in code → justify or remove
5. created_by/updated_by must always reflect the authenticated user — never "system"
6. Every K8s result must be scoped to environment + namespace — not stored globally
7. Design for future PostgreSQL migration — use standard SQL types
```

