## 4.2 `deployment_readiness` — Column Review & Naming

This is the table added in Bundle 1 to store per-environment, per-component K8s validation results.

### Issue: K8s Timestamps Must Be Environment-Scoped

Since this table already has `environment` and `namespace` as columns (and part of the composite key), the K8s sync timestamp here is implicitly scoped. **This is the correct place for K8s timestamps — not the components table.**

### Recommended `deployment_readiness` Table Structure

```sql
CREATE TABLE deployment_readiness (
    id                          BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,

    -- Composite Key Fields
    team_key                    VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    fix_version                 VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
    environment                 VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,        -- Test3 | Test4 | Stage-West | Production-East | Production-West
    namespace                   VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,       -- com-att-oc-fmo-test3
    component_name              VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,

    -- Branch Data
    release_branch              VARCHAR(255) NULL,           -- expected release branch (from components table)
    k8s_branch_raw              VARCHAR(255) NULL,           -- raw K8s label: release-26-07-28-rel
    k8s_branch_normalized       VARCHAR(255) NULL,           -- canonical: release/26.07.28.rel

    -- Commit Data
    k8s_commit_id               VARCHAR(40) NULL,            -- full SHA from K8s
    latest_release_commit_id    VARCHAR(40) NULL,            -- from components.release_branch_latest_commit_id

    -- Validation Results
    deployment_status           VARCHAR(50) NULL,            -- VALID | OLDER_BRANCH | NEEDS_REDEPLOYMENT | BRANCH_VALID_COMMIT_UNVERIFIED | UNABLE_TO_VALIDATE | USER_EXCLUDED
    validation_message          TEXT NULL,                   -- human-readable status message
    tooltip_message             TEXT NULL,                   -- detailed tooltip content

    -- Environment-Scoped K8s Sync Timestamps
    -- Named explicitly per environment type for clarity
    last_validated_at           TIMESTAMP NULL,              -- when this record was last refreshed
    k8s_sync_source             VARCHAR(50) NULL,            -- REFRESH | FORCE_REFRESH

    -- Audit
    created_by                  VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    created_date                TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_by                  VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    updated_date                TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,

    -- Composite Unique Key
    CONSTRAINT uq_deployment_readiness
        UNIQUE (team_key, fix_version, environment, namespace, component_name)
);
```

> **Regarding K8s timestamp naming (user request):**
> Since each row in `deployment_readiness` already has `environment` (e.g., "Production-East") and `namespace` columns, the `last_validated_at` timestamp is implicitly environment-specific. A record for "Production-East" / "com-att-oc-fmo-prod-east" has its own `last_validated_at`. This is cleaner than having separate `prod_east_sync_timestamp` and `prod_west_sync_timestamp` columns. The environment name in the row makes it self-documenting.

